From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:41:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: keep swap_pace clear of the tick
 boundaries

swap_pace held a J604 panel swap whose first reachable tick was one
between two 120 Hz refreshes until the swap was exactly the lead ahead of
that tick, which is the boundary itself: about half of the held swaps
still made that tick. Measured on the J604 with swap_pace on, frames still
landed on both phases of the refresh equally (150 and 152 of 302), with
the swap completions on one 4.17 ms grid to within 0.02 ms.

Pick the first grid tick the swap makes with a quarter tick to spare, and
start the swap only once the tick before it is out of reach by a quarter
tick as well. A lead off by up to a quarter tick then still lands the
frame on the grid, and the wait stays below one tick. Nothing changes
while swap_pace is off.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 9749f758bb50a9d9d1522a16780a926b4879e96f)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 2866b73866..40da61b4c6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -2624,35 +2624,42 @@ static bool dcp_m4_ext_swap_give_up(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, struct dcp_m4_swap
 
 /*
  * swap_pace: internal-panel swaps carry "as soon as possible" timing words,
- * so the panel shows a frame at its next 4.17 ms tick. Measured from the last
- * completion, even ticks are the 120 Hz grid and odd ones fall between two
- * refreshes. When the first tick a swap started now can make
- * (swap_pace_lead_us ahead) is an odd one, wait until it has passed, so the
- * frame is shown on the next grid tick instead. Returns the wait in us.
+ * so the panel shows a frame at the first 4.17 ms tick it can make. Measured
+ * from the last completion, even ticks are the 120 Hz grid and odd ones fall
+ * between two refreshes. A swap started now can make every tick at least the
+ * lead ahead (swap_pace_lead_us, or the learned floor). Pick the first grid
+ * tick it makes with a quarter tick to spare, and start only once the tick
+ * before it is out of reach by a quarter tick too, so that an error of up
+ * to a quarter tick in the lead still lands the frame on the grid. Returns
+ * the wait in us (less than one tick).
  */
 static unsigned long dcp_m4_swap_pace_us(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 {
-	u64 freq, half, base, now, t, k;
-	unsigned int lead;
+	u64 freq, half, margin, base, now, lead, k, start;
+	unsigned int lead_us;
 
 	if (!READ_ONCE(swap_pace))
 		return 0;
 	freq = arch_timer_get_cntfrq();
 	half = div_u64(freq, 240);
+	margin = half / 4;
 	base = READ_ONCE(r->int_done_cnt);
 	now = __arch_counter_get_cntpct();
 	if (!half || !base || base > now)
 		return 0;
-	lead = READ_ONCE(swap_pace_lead_us);
-	if (lead)
-		t = now + div_u64(freq * lead, USEC_PER_SEC);
+	lead_us = READ_ONCE(swap_pace_lead_us);
+	if (lead_us)
+		lead = div_u64(freq * lead_us, USEC_PER_SEC);
 	else
-		t = now + (READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq, 500));
-	k = div64_u64(t - base + half - 1, half);
-	if (!(k & 1))
+		lead = READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq, 500);
+	/* The first grid tick base + k * half (k even) at least lead + margin ahead. */
+	k = div64_u64(now + lead + margin - base + half - 1, half);
+	k += k & 1;
+	/* Start once the tick before it, base + (k - 1) * half, is out of reach by margin. */
+	start = base + (k - 1) * half + margin - lead;
+	if (start <= now)
 		return 0;
-	/* At most one tick (4.17 ms): the frame then makes tick k + 1. */
-	return div64_u64((base + k * half - t) * USEC_PER_SEC, freq) + 1;
+	return div64_u64((start - now) * USEC_PER_SEC, freq) + 1;
 }
 /*
  * The first timing word of an internal-panel swap (swap_target): 0 keeps the
-- 
